  {
    "objectID": "reports/hypoxic_extent.html#when-calendar-heatmap-from-interpolated-fields",
    "href": "reports/hypoxic_extent.html#when-calendar-heatmap-from-interpolated-fields",
    "title": "Hypoxic extent across cruises",
    "section": "When: calendar heatmap from interpolated fields",
    "text": "When: calendar heatmap from interpolated fields\nEach tile is a cruise week (ISO year × week). Color shows the shallowest hypoxic depth (m) in the interpolated oxygen field— the minimum depth at which O₂ falls below the threshold (default 2.0 mg/L, set via params.o2_threshold). Shallow hypoxia is yellow; deeper hypoxia is purple. Weeks with no hypoxia are left blank.\n\n\n\n\n\nShallowest hypoxic depth by cruise week from interpolated fields."
  },
  {
    "objectID": "reports/hypoxic_extent.html#when-hypoxic-extent-by-depth",
    "href": "reports/hypoxic_extent.html#when-hypoxic-extent-by-depth",
    "title": "Hypoxic extent across cruises",
    "section": "When: hypoxic extent by depth",
    "text": "When: hypoxic extent by depth\nEach row is a cruise; color is the percentage of CTD observations below the threshold in each depth bin.\n\n\n\n\n\nPercent of CTD observations below the hypoxic threshold at each depth."
  },
  {
    "objectID": "reports/hypoxic_extent.html#where-3d-hypoxic-volume",
    "href": "reports/hypoxic_extent.html#where-3d-hypoxic-volume",
    "title": "Hypoxic extent across cruises",
    "section": "Where: 3D hypoxic volume",
    "text": "Where: 3D hypoxic volume\nInteractive 3D view of hypoxic regions from interpolated fields, with BlueTopo bathymetry as the seafloor surface and coastline basemap lines at the sea surface. Each voxel shows the share of cruises with O₂ below the threshold at that location and depth (aligned to a common 4 m depth grid). Hypoxic volumes render at 60% opacity; non-hypoxic space is transparent. The color bar uses a log scale (1–100%). Drag to rotate, scroll to zoom."
  },
  {
    "objectID": "reports/hypoxic_extent.html#where-hypoxia-frequency-from-interpolated-fields",
    "href": "reports/hypoxic_extent.html#where-hypoxia-frequency-from-interpolated-fields",
    "title": "Hypoxic extent across cruises",
    "section": "Where: hypoxia frequency from interpolated fields",
    "text": "Where: hypoxia frequency from interpolated fields\nUse Prev / Next to step through ecological depth layers (same bins as the oxygen field maps). Color shows the log-scaled percentage of cruises whose interpolated field is hypoxic (O₂ below the threshold) at each grid cell within that layer."
